<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- INTERACTIVE URBAN WORLD for the paper drone (sim/interactive/app.py).

Layout: main road (N-S along x=0), cross road (E-W at y=-15), a building
cluster north, trees lining the roads, static cars + trucks on the roads,
street lamps, sidewalks, a helipad launch area at (0,-6).

Physics contract:
- the DRONE is the exact paper vehicle (mass 0.2 kg, paper inertia) -- same
  body as sim/mujoco/quadrotor.xml, visual extras exempt
- buildings / trees / vehicles / lamp poles / sidewalks have REAL collision
  geometry (named geoms, reported by the collision logger)
- roads, lane dashes, markings are visual-only thin plates
- interactive physics runs at 10 kHz (dt 1e-4): the repo's own analysis
  (empirically stable for fast-pole*dt < ~1.6; here 6150*1e-4 = 0.62)
  keeps the paper gains stable; the benchmark adapters keep 20 kHz + the
  strict 12.3 kHz assertion
-->
